#N canvas 20 20 2000 1900 12;
#X text 20 20 m_organelle -- the Organelle's OWN front panel \, mapped like any other device. mother.pd publishes aux and the four knobs on reserved names \; this turns them into named controls on param and disp \, and knows nothing about what any of them does. Same layer \, same rules and the same silence about meaning as m_nano. Everything about this module is on ref/device/organelle.md., f 58;
#X text 20 170 creation args: none. inlets: none. outlets: none., f 58;
#X obj 20 300 r aux;
#X obj 260 300 r knob1;
#X obj 500 300 r knob2;
#X obj 740 300 r knob3;
#X obj 980 300 r knob4;
#X obj 20 350 select 1;
#X obj 260 350 change -1;
#X obj 500 350 change -1;
#X obj 740 350 change -1;
#X obj 980 350 change -1;
#X msg 20 410 og-aux 1;
#X msg 260 410 og-knob-1 \$1;
#X msg 500 410 og-knob-2 \$1;
#X msg 740 410 og-knob-3 \$1;
#X msg 980 410 og-knob-4 \$1;
#X obj 20 520 t a a b;
#X obj 20 580 s disp;
#X obj 220 580 s param;
#X text 20 660 THE og- PREFIX IS NOT DECORATION. m_nano already publishes knob-1 to knob-9 \, and a single hyphen is not a distinction anyone can be trusted to read inside a route box. The Organelle's own knobs are og-knob-1 to og-knob-4 and its button is og-aux \, so the two surfaces can never be confused for one another. One line here if it reads badly on the screen., f 58;
#X text 20 820 PRESS ONLY \, like every button in this project. aux is momentary 1 then 0 \, so select 1 takes the press and its reject -- which carries the RELEASED 0 \, not a bang -- goes nowhere on purpose. What the press MEANS is u_map's business \, not this file's., f 58;
#X text 20 950 A MESSAGE BOX NEEDS NO list trim. og-knob-1 \$1 already has og-knob-1 as its SELECTOR \, which is the shape route matches -- so the list prepend / list trim chain that m_nano needs is simply absent here. In a message box \$1 is the incoming value \; in an object box it would be a creation argument., f 58;
#X text 640 520 FAN-IN NEEDS NO TRIGGER -- only a fan-out does. Five sources converge on one trigger \, which then does the fan-out. THE THIRD OUTLET IS PRESENCE \, added last and therefore rightmost \, so it fires FIRST: seen \, then param \, then disp. That order is not arbitrary -- mother having spoken at all is true whatever the value turns out to mean \, so it is the one claim that cannot be made wrong by anything below it. Action before report otherwise \, the same way u_init sequences its stages., f 44;
#X text 640 780 EVERY KNOB GOES THROUGH change -1. ✅ MOTHER PUSHES ONCE AT LOAD AND THEN SAYS NOTHING -- measured on the device 2026-08-08 \, one KNOB1 print in twelve seconds with nobody touching it. Item 237 \, and parameter pickup in u_map depends on it: if mother streamed \, the first value would be spent on its own reading and pickup would never arm. THE -1 IS LOAD-BEARING: a bare change starts life holding 0 \, so a knob physically parked at 0 would never publish at all and the tempo would sit at its default. -1 cannot be a real value here \, since mother's knobs are 0 to 1. Measured \, not reasoned -- the bare form swallowed the first value in testing, f 60;
#X text 640 1060 WHAT IS NOT HERE: the encoder \, encbut \, the keyboard and the pedal jack. The encoder is contested with mother's own menu through enableSubMenu \, and none of the others has anything to drive yet. They belong in THIS file when they do -- it is one device \, so it is one m_ abstraction., f 44;
#X text 20 1250 ⛔ THE KNOBS NO LONGER REPORT TO disp \, and og-aux still does. A knob's RAW 0-to-1 position is not a readable parameter row -- the screen said og-knob-1 0.245 where a BPM belonged \, and the param layer replaces the footer \, so the tempo it was mapped to vanished while you turned it. u_map reports the value instead \, because it is the only file that knows what a control MEANS: the mapped value when there is a mapping and the raw one when there is not. ⚠️ AN UNMAPPED KNOB STILL REPORTS \, and an earlier version of this comment claimed the opposite. A control that does nothing and says nothing cannot be told from a broken one. Item 242. ⚠️ og-aux keeps its own report because the transport is not a mapped value, f 62;
#X msg 440 560 seen m_organelle;
#X obj 440 620 s presence;
#X obj 1000 1200 loadbang;
#X msg 1000 1260 expect m_organelle passive;
#X obj 1000 1320 s presence;
#X text 1100 950 LIVENESS OFF THE FAN-IN \, WHICH IS THE ONLY PLACE IT COULD GO. There is no channel gate here and no reply to match -- mother publishes on reserved global names and this file simply receives them \, so the arrival of ANY of the five IS the evidence. ⚠️ It is weaker evidence than the other two devices give \, and the kind field says so., f 40;
#X text 1000 1400 ⛔ PASSIVE IS A KIND ON THE PRESENCE BUS \, NOT A SILENCE. m_organelle registers itself and publishes seen \, and it instantiates NO c_presence -- so nothing ages it and it can never be declared lost. ✅ MOTHER PUSHES THE KNOBS ONCE AT LOAD AND THEN SAYS NOTHING -- item 237 \, measured -- so a last-heard clock here would run out a few seconds into EVERY boot and put a device-lost warning on the screen for hardware that is bolted to the instrument. What a passive layer can offer is LAST HEARD \, which is plan-v03.5's diagnostic screen. What it cannot offer is the difference between unplugged and untouched \, and no amount of code here changes that -- the operator supplies it. See ref/module/presence.md., f 44;
